y in patients with cirrhosis</article-title><source>J Hepatol</source><year>1999</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>890</fpage><lpage>895</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10365817</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b6-tcrm-5-617"><label>6</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ferenci</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lockwood</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Mullen</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Hepatic encephalopathy&#x02013;definition, nomenclature, diagnosis, and quantification: final report of the working party at the 11th World Congresses of Gastroenterology, Vienna, 1998</article-title><source>Hepatology</source><year>2002</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>716</fpage><lpage>721</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11870389</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b7-tcrm-5-617"><label>7</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blei</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cordoba</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Practice Parameters Committee of the American College of Gastroenterology: Hepatic encephalopathy</article-title><source>Am J Gastroenterol</source><year>2001</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>1968</fpage><lpage>1976</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11467622</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-tcrm-5-617"><label>8</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mendler</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Donovan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Blei</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Yamada</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Alpers</surname><given-names>D</g