lism in patients with cirrhosis</article-title><source>Hepatology</source><year>2004</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>73</fpage><lpage>79</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15239088</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-tcrm-5-617"><label>12</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O&#x02019;Carroll</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayes</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ebmeier</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Regional cerebral blood flow and cognitive function in patients with chronic liver disease</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1991</year><volume>337</volume><fpage>1250</fpage><lpage>1253</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1674063</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-tcrm-5-617"><label>13</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stahl</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Studies of the blood ammonia in liver disease: Its diagnostic, prognostic, and therapeutic significance</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>1963</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>24</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13978712</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-tcrm-5-617"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blei</surname><given-names>AT</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Bircher</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Benhamou</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>McIntyre</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Rizzetto</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Rod&#x000e9;s</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hepatic encephalopathy</article-title><source>Oxford Textbook of Clinical Hepatology</source><edition>2nd Ed</edition><publisher-loc>Oxford, UK</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Oxford Medical</publisher-name><year>1999</year><fpage>765</fpage><lpage>783</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-tcrm-5-617"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>C&#x000f3;rdoba</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Blei</surname><given-names>AT</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Schiff</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name><name><surname>Sorrell</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Maddrey</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hepatic encephalopathy</article-title><source>Schiff&#x02019;s Diseases of the Liver</source><publisher-loc>Philadelphia, PA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Lippincott Williams &#x00026; Wilkins</publisher-name><year>2003</year><fpage>595</fpage><lpage>623</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16-tcrm-5-617"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Butterworth</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The neurobiology of hepatic encephalopathy</article-title><source>Semin Liver Dis</source><year>1996</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>235</fpage><lpage>244</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8989809</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b17-tcrm-5-617"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ahboucha</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Butterworth</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pathophysiology of hepatic encephalopathy: A new look at GABA from the molecular standpoint</article-title><source>Metab Brain Dis</source><year>2